","cnm_148"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p148","cnm_p089"],"id":"equal-area-partition","label":"Equal areas under folding","methodDirectNodeIds":{"equal-area-partition":["cnm_192","cnm_p150"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_192","cnm_p150","cnm_p148","cnm_p089"]}],"status":"mapped","supportIds":["cnm_132","cnm_p077","cnm_174","cnm_055","cnm_042"],"version":"1.0.0"},"level":"Middle school","number":4,"question":"A rectangular sheet of paper \\(ABCD\\) has \\(AB=8\\) and \\(BC=10\\) (the vertices are in the order \\(A,B,C,D\\)). Fold it along \\(AE\\) so that point \\(D\\) lands exactly at point \\(F\\) on side \\(BC\\), with point \\(E\\) on \\(CD\\). Find the length of \\(CE\\).\n\n[Figure 1](figures/cnm_176_q4_question_en.svg)","questionType":"mixed","rejectedAnswers":[],"responseType":"numeric","schemaVersion":"3.0","skill":[],"solution":"\\(AF=AD=10\\), \\(BF=\\sqrt{10^2-8^2}=6\\), and \\(FC=4\\). Let \\(CE=x\\). Then \\(EF=DE=8-x\\). In right triangle \\(ECF\\), \\(x^2+4^2=(8-x)^2\\). Solving gives \\(x=3\\).","solutionAvailability":"present","solutionMethods":[{"directNodeIds":["cnm_192","cnm_148"],"explanation":"\\(AF=AD=10\\), \\(BF=\\sqrt{10^2-8^2}=6\\), and \\(FC=4\\). Let \\(CE=x\\). Then \\(EF=DE=8-x\\). In right triangle \\(ECF\\), \\(x^2+4^2=(8-x)^2\\). Solving gives \\(x=3\\).","id":"pythagorean-equation","label":"Pythagorean equation","legacyRouteId":"solution:pythagorean-equation:0885725350a7","provenance":{"contribution":"Existing attributed explanation retained; project contribution is review and annotations.","evidence":[{"label":"Accepted primary worked-solution review","path":"../database/knowledge-graph/evidence/cn-solutions-2026-11-06/cnm_176_q4.json","sha256":"e875e201521f5363db64ff71a7c8e4c157bee44b03087c981beda71f9c5a3694"}],"license":"CC-BY-NC-4.0","licenseURL":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/","reviewStatus":"Current explanation retained and independently AI-reviewed; not teacher reviewed","source":"cn-math-taxonomy (AI-generated; not teacher reviewed)","sourceRef":"cn-math/cnm_176_q4#pythagorean-equation","sourceRevision":"62b341d4b66b175413d6e3f697e37639fd96aa2d","sourceURL":"https://github.com/xiaoyang111222/cn-math-taxonomy"}},{"directNodeIds":["cnm_192","cnm_p150"],"explanation":"The fold fixes \\(A\\) and \\(E\\) and sends triangle \\(ADE\\) to triangle \\(AFE\\), so their areas are equal and \\(AF=AD=10\\). In right triangle \\(ABF\\), \\(BF=\\sqrt{10^2-8^2}=6\\), giving \\(CF=10-6=4\\).\n\nJoin \\(AF\\) and \\(EF\\). Together with \\(AE\\), they divide the rectangle into triangles \\(ABF\\), \\(AFE\\), \\(ADE\\), and \\(ECF\\), with no overlapping interiors. Let \\(x=CE\\), where \\(0\\le x\\le8\\). Since \\(DE=8-x\\), triangles \\(ADE\\) and \\(AFE\\) each have area \\(10(8-x)/2\\). The other two areas are \\(8\\cdot6/2=24\\) and \\(4x/2=2x\\). Adding the four areas gives\n\\[\n80=24+2\\cdot\\frac{10(8-x)}2+2x=104-8x.\n\\]\nThus \\(x=3\\), which lies in the required interval, so \\(CE=3\\).","id":"equal-area-partition","label":"Equal areas under folding","legacyRouteId":"equal-area-partition","provenance":{"contribution":"New project-authored alternative alongside the retained attributed explanation.","evidence":[{"label":"Accepted primary worked-solution review","path":"../database/knowledge-graph/evidence/cn-solutions-2026-11-06/cnm_176_q4.json","sha256":"e875e201521f5363db64ff71a7c8e4c157bee44b03087c981beda71f9c5a3694"}],"license":"CC-BY-NC-4.0","licenseURL":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/","reviewStatus":"AI-authored and independently AI-reviewed; not teacher reviewed","source":"Math Practice alternative method","sourceRef":"cn-math/cnm_176_q4#equal-area-partition","sourceURL":"https://github.com/rqzhu-aide/math-practice"}},{"directNodeIds":["cnm_174","cnm_271","cnm_272"],"id":"similar-right-triangles","label":"Similar right triangles","legacyRouteId":"similar-right-triangles","provenance":{"evidence":[{"label":"Legacy graph and grading review","path":"../database/knowled